# Proxy the API to Render. These are rewrites (status 200), not redirects, so
# the browser still sees one origin — which keeps the session cookie first-party
# and sidesteps CORS entirely. Safari blocks third-party cookies by default, so
# calling Render directly from the browser would break sessions on iOS.
#
# Order matters: the SPA catch-all must stay last, or it swallows these.
/api/*       https://spotify-party-room.onrender.com/api/:splat       200
/spotify/*   https://spotify-party-room.onrender.com/spotify/:splat   200

# Spotify's OAuth callback. Kept on the Netlify origin so the session cookie set
# during /spotify/get-auth-url is still attached when the state is verified.
/callback    https://spotify-party-room.onrender.com/callback         200

# Client-side routes: /room/:code, /join, /create are React Router's, not files.
/*           /index.html                                              200
